---
import Content from '../layouts/Content.astro';
import { company, offers, publicDeployment as deployment } from '../data/site';
---
<Content
  title={`Plan an AI workload | ${company.full}`}
  description="Prepare your AI workload, tenancy, data, performance and delivery requirements for a SmartTec deployment review. Planned services; procurement and commissioning ahead."
  kicker="Workload planner / From requirements to proposal"
  heading="Define the job. Design the deployment."
  lede="Start with the application and the service your customers need. We turn that brief into a workload validation plan, hardware configuration and commercial proposal, with a clear path through procurement and commissioning."
  meta={[
    { label: 'Fleet proposal', value: deployment.label, note: deployment.systemLabel, tone: 'signal' },
    { label: 'Launch power', value: 'Grid first', note: 'Solar and BESS in a later phase' },
    { label: 'Service stage', value: 'Planned', note: 'No commissioned capacity offered' },
    { label: 'Next step', value: 'Technical review', note: 'Configuration and terms by proposal' },
  ]}
>
  <section aria-labelledby="planner" data-reveal>
    <p class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow__n">01</span><span class="eyebrow__t">Choose the service</span></p>
    <h2 id="planner">Ownership and tenancy come first.</h2>
    <div class="cards">{offers.map(offer => <article class="card"><h3>{offer.name}</h3><p>{offer.summary}</p></article>)}</div>
    <p>Shared inference and dedicated GPU servers use different scheduling and isolation designs. Tell us whether you need shared inference or a dedicated single-tenant node on SmartTec-owned hardware, or colocation for your own equipment.</p>
  </section>
  <section aria-labelledby="brief" data-reveal>
    <p class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow__n">02</span><span class="eyebrow__t">Prepare the brief</span></p>
    <h2 id="brief">The details that shape a useful proposal.</h2>
    <dl class="spec">
      <div><dt>Application and models</dt><dd>Inference, rendering or another workload<span class="note">Include model/version, license, precision, context length, expected request mix and the software you intend to run.</span></dd></div>
      <div><dt>Performance</dt><dd>Define the customer outcome<span class="note">Latency, throughput, concurrent requests, batch sizes, scheduled hours and peak periods establish the benchmark to run.</span></dd></div>
      <div><dt>Data and access</dt><dd>Storage, networking and isolation<span class="note">Include dataset size, transfer patterns, private networking, access controls, retention and any compliance requirements.</span></dd></div>
      <div><dt>Hardware ownership</dt><dd>Your equipment or SmartTec-owned servers<span class="note">For colocation, include rack dimensions, weight, power connections and the equipment's cooling specification.</span></dd></div>
      <div><dt>Service responsibilities</dt><dd>Agree who operates each layer<span class="note">Specify software administration, patching, monitoring, support coverage and recovery requirements before a service commitment.</span></dd></div>
      <div><dt>Commercial scope</dt><dd>Target date, duration and usage commitment<span class="note">A proposed start date depends on customer terms, equipment delivery and facility acceptance. An inquiry does not reserve capacity.</span></dd></div>
    </dl>
  </section>
  <section aria-labelledby="validation" data-reveal>
    <p class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow__n">03</span><span class="eyebrow__t">Validate before deployment</span></p>
    <h2 id="validation">A benchmark connects the model to the machine.</h2>
    <div class="split"><p>Memory capacity alone does not determine throughput or service quality. A representative workload test will establish the supported configuration, scheduling approach and performance envelope. Electrical and cooling review must then confirm that the facility can support it.</p><p>The current proposal is {deployment.gpus} B300 GPUs in {deployment.systems} complete Supermicro systems. The 60 modeled saleable GPUs and four held back are a financial allocation, not a complete standby node or a validated tenant layout. Customer discussions remain unsigned and procurement is ahead.</p></div>
    <div class="actions"><a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/compute">Review the proposed fleet</a><a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/power">Review power and cooling</a></div>
  </section>
  <section class="is-end" aria-labelledby="next" data-reveal>
    <p class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow__n">04</span><span class="eyebrow__t">Start a conversation</span></p>
    <h2 id="next">Bring the brief to SmartTec.</h2>
    <p>Share the requirements you know, and we can work through the rest together. Detailed project economics and their assumptions are available separately in the protected investor area.</p>
    <div class="actions"><a class="btn" href="/contact">Request a deployment review</a><a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/investors">Open the investor area</a></div>
  </section>
</Content>
